From {{etyl|de|bs}} {{term|Marzipan|lang=de}}, earlier {{term|marcipan}}, a misinterpretation of {{etyl|it|bs}} {{term|marzapane|lang=it}} (as if from Latin {{term|Marci|lang=la}} {{term|panis|lang=la}} ‘Mark's bread’), now thought originally to come from [[w:Martaban|Martaban]], a Burmese port known for its spice exports.

